From: E87N Armbian port <local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: give E87N GMACs stable Ethernet aliases

The MTK driver assigns each netdev its MAC node as dev.of_node. With the
v257 naming scheme, systemd net_id can use aliases of these per-port nodes
to produce distinct ID_NET_NAME_ONBOARD values (end0 and end1). The existing
persistent MAC policy can then use board port identity instead of the
enumeration-dependent ethN fallback.

Keep net.ifnames=0 in the image's existing boot arguments to retain primary
interface names. No fixed MAC, extra link policy or runtime writer is added.
This supplies source-level identity support; board boot validation is pending.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7987a-edgepi-e87n.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7987a-edgepi-e87n.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7987a-edgepi-e87n.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7987a-edgepi-e87n.dts
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
 
 	aliases {
 		serial0 = &uart0;
+		ethernet0 = &gmac0;
+		ethernet1 = &gmac1;
 	};
 
 	chosen {
